msgid "No. The check is a browser-side proof of work, so it only runs on real form submissions in a browser. XML-RPC and the REST API are not browsers, so they are left untouched and a captcha cannot gate them. If you do not use XML-RPC, disabling it separately closes that brute-force surface."
